The de Broglie wavelength formula is given by:

\[
\lambda = \frac{h}{p}
\]

where \( p = mv \) is the momentum of the particle.

---

**(a) Truck:**
- Mass \( m = 10,000 \, \text{kg} \)
- Velocity \( v = 27.8 \, \text{m/s} \)
- Momentum \( p = 10,000 \times 27.8 = 278,000 \, \text{kg·m/s} \)
- Wavelength \( \lambda = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34}}{278,000} \approx 2.4 \times 10^{-37} \, \text{cm} \)

---

**(b) Flea:**
- Mass \( m = 50 \, \text{mg} = 50 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{kg} \)
- Velocity \( v = 1 \, \text{m/s} \)
- Momentum \( p = 50 \times 10^{-6} \times 1 = 50 \times 10^{-6} \, \text{kg·m/s} \)
- Wavelength \( \lambda = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34}}{50 \times 10^{-6}} \approx 1.3 \times 10^{-27} \, \text{cm} \)

