For a signal \( S_a(200t) \), the frequency is 100 Hz (since the argument is \(200t\), the angular frequency is \(200\) rad/s, which corresponds to \(100\) Hz). The Nyquist rate is twice the highest frequency, so:

\[
\text{Nyquist rate} = 2 \times 100 = 200 \text{ samples per second (cps)}
\]

The Nyquist interval is the reciprocal of the Nyquist rate:

\[
